diff --git a/man/greetd-5.scd b/man/greetd-5.scd
index 29b7045..68adea6 100644
--- a/man/greetd-5.scd
+++ b/man/greetd-5.scd
@@ -47,6 +47,21 @@ This section contains terminal configuration.
 
 	Default is true.
 
+*text_mode* = true|false
+	Whether or not to set *vt* to text mode before starting a session.
+
+	Text mode lets textual sessions, such as a shell, show on the VT. If set to
+	false, a session finds the VT in the mode it was left in: a graphical session
+	can then take over a VT that something else, such as a boot splash, left in
+	graphics mode, without the console showing in between, but a textual session
+	started on a VT in graphics mode shows nothing.
+
+	Whatever this is set to, greetd sets *vt* to text mode, and its keyboard to
+	Unicode mode, before it exits because it could not start the greeter or a
+	session, or because the greeter exited without starting one.
+
+	Default is true.
+
